C4. MULTIPLIER FROM THE WALK, NOT DIVISION -- MET
  Read diff (`rtk proxy git diff HEAD -- internal/services/metrics/metrics.go`):
  TargetProvenance calls `mult, name, straddles := phaseWalk(s, rangeStart, rangeEnd)`
  and stores mult directly; there is no target/base division anywhere in the file.
  phaseAdjustedMonthlyTarget is now `avgMultiplier, _, _ := phaseWalk(...); return
  base * avgMultiplier` -- one walk implementation, two callers.
  Zero-base sentinel probe output:
    "PROBE zero-base: target=0 provenance={Base:0 Multiplier:0 PhaseName:
     Straddles:false Annotate:false}"
    "PROBE zero-base: target/base (division approach) = NaN ; walk multiplier = 0"
  i.e. no division by zero, Multiplier finite, Annotate false (not annotated).
  Straddle probe (base 7386, ages 64/74/84, 24-month range) confirms
