  OBSERVATION on "byte-identical visible card": the raw HTML is NOT byte-identical
  in the unannotated case. `diff -u old.html new.html` shows exactly two changes
  inside the Monthly Living Expenses card:
      +                 (three blank lines from the new {{if}} template actions)
      -  Target <span class="num">$2,000.00</span> ...
      +  <span>Target <span class="num">$2,000.00</span></span> ...
  i.e. an attribute-less wrapper <span> is emitted even when Annotate is false
  (kpis.html only makes title/aria-label conditional, not the span itself).
  A bare inline <span> with no attributes and no CSS carries no visual or
  assistive-tech effect, and criterion 6 as written tests *visible text*, which
  is byte-identical. Recorded here so the lead can judge whether the brief's
  "byte-identical visible card" was meant more strictly than that.

